From ee8423cdebe7b4a53b1ec9507c849e036405fce6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:36:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): a milling operation is never posted on a lathe's
 work spindle

A lathe post opens every section that states no C angle with the WORK
spindle (G97 S M03). The stream names no operation family, so a milling
pass that stays on one meridian - a Face pass with an end mill along
Y = 0 - read to fanuc-lathe.cps and tormach-lathe.cps like a facing pass
and posted the work spindle at the cutter's rpm with the cutter standing
still.

The program gate now decides it before a line is written, from what it
already holds (the operation's kind, its cached path, its work offset):
through a turning dialect a section passes only as live-tool work (its
path states C), a turning-family kind, or a Drill whose every cutting
move and cycle is on the spindle axis with the tool along +Z (how a
lathe drills and taps on centre). Every other operation is refused by
name. `app::lathe_voice::voice` is the one derivation; `at_post` is the
door, called by the single-file, per-mount and per-operation posts, so
the GUI, the script verb and the MCP tool all take it. A mill post is
untouched.

The dialect is read from the script's own manifest (`capabilities`, the
mask every shipped post already states) by `post::dialect::speaks_turning`;
`post::dialect::states_live_tool` is the one "does the path state C?"
test, and the stream's PARAM LiveTool is written from it. No change to
the stream format, the CL spec or any post script; goldens unchanged.

Pinned by lathe_voice's unit table over every operation kind and by the
lathe_work_spindle suite (both reproductions, every post entry point).

Fixes #1190

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
